ing drill-down or access scope."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Shows best/worst lots and makes comparison basis apparent, without requiring supporting-record drill-down."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":3,"summary":"Allows users to open summaries and inspect underlying records; restricts dashboards and financial details by authorized access."}],"span":"I-9","topic":"Dashboard drill-down and data access"},{"id":"D-18","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Provides filtered lot comparisons without specifying yard or financial access restrictions."},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":2,"summary":"Provides multi-lot comparisons without specifying access restrictions."},{"behaviour":5,"sketch":3,"summary":"Restricts reports and exports to authorized yards/lots and applies profitability access restrictions."}],"span":"I-10","topic":"Report access controls"},{"id":"D-19","readings":[{"behaviour":2,"sketch":1,"summary":"Keeps sample data distinct and warns or prevents duplicate loading."},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":2,"summary":"Provides sample data, without specifying loading, reset, or duplication controls."},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":3,"summary":"Allows authorized users to load or reset sample data, with confirmation for destructive replacement and failure reporting."}],"span":"I-11","topic":"Sample-data loading and lifecycle"},{"id":"D-20","readings":[{"behaviour":1,"sketch":1,"summary":"Shows the summary and updates it when underlying records change, without specifying access scope or data-availability qualification."},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Recomputes from active-lot data and indicates no active lots or uncalculable metrics."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":3,"summary":"Shows contributing period and data availability, and limits the yard summary to users with yard access."}],"span":"I-11","topic":"Yard-summary access and data qualification"},{"id":"D-21","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Calls for a usable web-app demo, prompt overview, validation results, challenges, readiness assessment, and mock-data limitations."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":2,"summary":"Requires a demonstrable responsive web app with representative sample data and a walkthrough of observable results."},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":3,"summary":"Requires a working responsive demo demonstrating procurement through feeding and performance reporting, plus explicit limits when a workflow cannot be demonstrated."}],"span":"I-12","topic":"Demo and presentation deliverables"}],"round":1,"sketches":[{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"When an authorized user imports procurement and receiving records, create or update records for purchase orders, PO lines, vendors, costs, head counts, animal weights, and receiving details; show an import result identifying accepted and rejected rows."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Let the user associate each PO line with one or more lots and lots with pens, including pen capacity and current animal count; retain the PO-line-to-lot-to-pen links so a lot split across multiple lots remains traceable."},{"kind":"error","text":"Show an error for malformed or incomplete rows, duplicate records, or references that cannot be matched; do not silently create incomplete mappings or overwrite existing data without indicating the conflict."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only users with operational access can import records or change PO, lot, and pen mappings; users without that access cannot make those changes."}],"id":"I-1","readingChosen":"Treat “import” as synchronization of both PO and receiving data, and support one PO line mapping to multiple lots as well as one-to-one mapping, with traceability preserved through pens."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"On receipt of animal weight and lot data, show a target weight and projected market date for each lot using its entry weight, configured target weight, and a configured expected gain rate; show the inputs used for the forecast."},{"kind":"happy","text":"When new lot weight